<%# Placeholder for a lazily-loaded turbo-frame, in place of the line of text
    these frames used to show. Ui::SkeletonComponent existed, was tested, and
    was used by nothing but its own preview (DS-05).

    The bars are aria-hidden (the component sets that itself), so the label
    still carries the meaning for anyone who is not looking at the shape: the
    wrapper announces itself as a status region and names what is loading.

    `rows` is how many field-shaped pairs to draw — enough to fill the frame
    without pretending to know the form's exact shape. %>
<div role="status" class="flex min-h-24 flex-col justify-center gap-3 py-2">
  <span class="sr-only"><%= label %></span>
  <% local_assigns.fetch(:rows, 2).times do %>
    <%= render Ui::SkeletonComponent.new(class_name: "h-3 w-24") %>
    <%= render Ui::SkeletonComponent.new(class_name: "h-9 w-full") %>
  <% end %>
</div>
